message: "If you use these skills in research or products, please cite the repository and the underlying method authors named in each SKILL.md."
title: "structured-analytic-skills: structured analytic techniques as agent skills"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-18"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/radarist/structured-analytic-skills"
authors:
  - family-names: Babelis
    given-names: Claudio
keywords:
  - structured analytic techniques
  - agent skills
  - intelligence analysis
  - foresight
  - evidence appraisal
  - decision support
abstract: >-
  A library of agent skills that implement published analytic methods (Heuer's ACH,
  NATO Admiralty grading, GRADE, Cochrane RoB 2, Delphi, scenario planning, Wardley
  mapping, NASA TRL, Brier scoring, meta-analysis and others), each with citations,
  worked examples, verification checklists, and deterministic companion tools, plus a
  deterministic multidimensional scorer for the library itself.
